sparky-stereo-model-viewer (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depends: qml6-module-org-kde-desktop and qml6-module-qtquick (ORDER 750 finding). The program sets the Qt Quick Controls style
    org.kde.desktop itself (src/main.cpp) when QT_QUICK_CONTROLS_STYLE is empty, and the style's module is a package of its own
    (source kf6-qqc2-desktop-style); without it the window stays black with "module org.kde.desktop is not installed". Every
    import of the QML files now has its package named: org.kde.kirigami (qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami), QtQuick (qml6-module-qtquick),
    QtQuick.Controls, QtQuick.Dialogs, QtQuick.Layouts (qml6-module-qtquick-controls, -dialogs, -layouts), QtQuick.Templates through
    the Controls (qml6-module-qtquick-templates, already named).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0300

sparky-stereo-model-viewer (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libf3d's window is made by F3D's automatic backend (engine::create), not createGLX(): createGLX loads libGLX.so, the unversioned development
    symlink, so the viewer stopped at start with "Cannot find GLX library" on a system without libglx-dev (found in a Plasma login rig that
    had none; the earlier rigs had the symlink). ORDER 17 milestone 7 round 3.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:30:00 -0300

sparky-stereo-model-viewer (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release (ORDER 17 milestone 7): a Kirigami window with libf3d's 3D area, a declared stereo surface whose depth is the person's limits.

